"""Paper-by-paper literature data.

Single source of truth for: Section 14 (paper-by-paper analysis), the comparison
matrix (Section 13), and artifacts/literature_review.xlsx / .csv.

Matrix vocabulary (definitions are printed in the document):
  Few-shot      Yes = main evaluation uses <=10 normal (or labelled) samples per category
                Partial = a low-shot experiment or few references, but not the main setting
  Rotation      Yes = explicitly models AND evaluates rotation / orientation change
                Partial = handles alignment or uses augmentation, no controlled rotation test
  Localization  Yes = pixel / region output evaluated against ground truth
                Partial = maps or boxes produced, limited evaluation
  Unknown       Yes = separates unknown anomalies from known defect classes
                Partial = flags any deviation from normal, but has no known-class concept
  Feedback      Yes = learns from human / verified feedback
                Partial = continual or incremental learning without a human verification loop
Values: Yes, Partial, No, Not evaluated, Unclear.

Results are only quoted when the number was confirmed in the abstract or the
official record during this session. Otherwise the field says what was reported
in words and asks the reader to check the tables.
"""

